@ ---- LBL :REC: the record of the stop R32 (XEQ IND 32): R28 the offset, R29 the column; the label
@ stores its cities in R72-R74 (texts of up to 196 characters) and the numbers R75 (the cities in R72),
@ R76 (in R72 and R73), R77 (all). Then its first city (R80 = 1) ----
LBL 58                          ; :REC:
XEQ 85                          ; -> :RECX:
1
STO 80
@
@ ---- LBL :CITY: the city R80 of the stop: its entry "rCCname" (r the DST rule letter, CC the country)
@ taken out of R72, R73 or R74 (R82 its place there) into R78 with the "/" between the entries:
@ R50 the rule (the place of r in R81: 0 none, 1-26 LBL 40 + r, 27 irregular), R84 the country, R48 the name ----
LBL 59                          ; :CITY:
RCL 80
STO 82
RCL 72
STO 78
RCL 75
RCL 80
X>Y?
XEQ 60                          ; -> :PART2:
RCL 76
RCL 80
X>Y?
XEQ 61                          ; -> :PART3:
"/"
x→α 78
@ the entries before it off: each time the text up to its first "/" off (αSL)
DO 03
  RCL 82
  1
  X<Y?
WHILE 03
  "/"
  αPOS 78
  1
  +
  αSL 78
  1
  STO- 82
ENDDO 03
"/"
αPOS 78
αLEFT 78
STO 78
1
αLEFT 78
αPOS 81
STO 50
1
αSL 78
2
αLEFT 78
STO 84
2
αSL 78
RCL 78
STO 48
RTN
@ LBL :PART2:, LBL :PART3: the city is in R73 (place - R75) or R74 (place - R76)
LBL 60                          ; :PART2:
RCL 73
STO 78
RCL 80
RCL 75
-
STO 82
RTN
LBL 61                          ; :PART3:
RCL 74
STO 78
RCL 80
RCL 76
-
STO 82
RTN
@
@ ---- LBL :CUP: the city before (1 -> the last), LBL :CDOWN: the city after (the last -> 1); the header ----
LBL 62                          ; :CUP:
RCL 80
1
-
X=0?
RCL 77
STO 80
XEQ 59                          ; -> :CITY:
XEQ 72                          ; -> :HEAD:
RTN
LBL 63                          ; :CDOWN:
RCL 80
RCL 77
