@ ---- LBL :NOWOFF: R59 = the offset of the city now: R28, + R49 when its rule R50 has DST on at the UT
@ R31 (rule 0 or 27: none, R49 = 0). The rule (LBL 40 + r) pushes the end hour, the end code, the start
@ hour, the start code + 20000 x DST (h); a code
@ is 100 month + 10 n + weekday (n 1-4, 5 the last; weekday 0 Sunday), the hours in standard time.
@ R53 the start, R54 the end (JDs in the stop's standard time) in the year of R57 = R31 + R28/24 (the stop's standard time now) ----
LBL 64                          ; :NOWOFF:
RCL 28
STO 59
0
STO 49
RCL 50
X=0?
RTN
27
X=Y?
RTN
RCL 28
24
÷
